WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/battery/pages/EnergyProductsPage.tsx — owns FOUR data sources:
    useTeslaEnergySites (GET /tesla/energy-sites) + useRefreshTeslaEnergySites (POST …/refresh),
    useTeslaEnergySiteInfo (GET …/{siteId}/site-info) + useRefreshTeslaEnergySiteInfo (POST …/site-info/refresh).
  It renders a PageContainer (title "Energy Products" + subtitle + "Refresh from Tesla" action), a four-up summary
  StatCard row (Energy Sites / With Solar / With Battery / Backup Capable), and a StaggerContainer grid of EnergySiteCards.
  Each EnergySiteCard (GlassPanel) = header(resource icon + name + resource·id + battery_type Badge) → 3 StatCards
  (Charge `fmtNumber(pct,1)%` / Capacity `fmtEnergy(total_pack_energy)` / Type `resourceLabel`) → CapBadge row
  (Solar/Battery/Grid/Backup/Storm Watch + Storm-Mode-Active) → SiteInfoSection → footer("Last fetched …").
  SiteInfoSection = header("Site Configuration" + refresh) → Operation Mode + Backup Reserve(RadialGauge, max 100) →
  StatCards(Powerwalls=battery_count, Rated Power=fmtPower(nameplate_power), Rated Energy=fmtEnergy(nameplate_energy),
  each guarded `!= null`) → firmware+timezone → component badges → TOU Rate-Plan box(name | "No rate plan" + Update) →
  "Site info fetched …" timestamp; with an EmptyState when info==null. Helpers: fmtEnergy/fmtPower use a `>= 1000`
  kWh/kW ladder (1-dp) else Wh/W (0-dp); fmtNumber = locale decimal w/ safeNumber(non-finite→0); formatDateTime →
  med date + time, '—' on null/invalid; resourceLabel/operationModeLabel are hardcoded English enum maps.

