PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift)
  The generated prompt names the output apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**. The repo's XcodeGen spec (project.yml,
  both app targets) AND .swiftlint.yml `included` reference apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/ — where ALL 1438 sibling
  P4 feature-views live (including the direct ancestors EnergySummaryPanel + BatteryTab). The predecessor P4 log
  (p4-apple-feature-views-0142-EnergySummaryPanel) records this as the convention ("project.yml + .swiftlint.yml already
  include TeslaSync/feature-views"). Shipping into a non-compiled, non-linted Features/Battery/ would make the page fail
  the build + lint it is meant to pass. Per "No predecessor bypass", the surface ships in feature-views/ (compiled +
  linted + convention-consistent); navigation registration uses the shell's documented AppRouteHostRegistry seam. The
  multi-file split (Adapter/Projection/Model/View/Views/SiteCard/RatePlan/Previews/Registration/Tests) matches the exact
  sibling convention and keeps every file ≤ 400 lines (swiftlint --strict file_length).

PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  PageContainer/GlassPanel  → TSGlassPanel · StatCard → TSStatCard · Badge → TSBadge/TSIconBox · Button → TSButton ·
  RadialGauge → TSRadialGauge (P3 Swift-Charts wrapper) · EmptyState → TSEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView) ·
  Skeleton → TSSkeleton · FadeIn/Stagger → TSFadeIn/TSStaggerContainer/TSStaggerItem · QueryError → TSQueryError.
  fmtEnergy/fmtPower (>=1000 ladder) → EnergyProductsFormat.energy/power · fmtNumber → EnergyProductsFormat.number ·
  formatDateTime → EnergyProductsFormat.dateTime · resourceLabel/operationModeLabel → EnergyProductsLabels (i18n keys,
  not hardcoded English) · colours/typography/spacing → Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius (no raw hex).
  i18n  : every visible string is a LocalizedStringKey resolved from Localizable.xcstrings; only unit symbols (kWh/Wh/
          kW/W/%) and data passthroughs (site name, server component keys) are verbatim — exactly as the web hardcodes.
  a11y  : panels/cards .accessibilityElement + labels; the gauge carries label+value; refresh buttons have labels;
          headers .isHeader; Dynamic Type via tokens; light/dark via Color.TS dynamic colours.
  units : SI in / display at the boundary — Powerwall energy/power are site-native SI figures shown with SI symbols,
          the same way the web source renders them (no conversion in the page).
  state : loading (skeleton cards + per-card skeletons) · empty (no products / no site config) · error (sites query
          failure + Retry; per-card site-info failure + retry) · data (summary + cards). Plus the freshness chip/banner
          + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition.

